Task 4 – File and Exception Forensics (7 Marks)
4.1 Locate the defects
• Opening returns.log in w mode truncates the existing log every time save_returns() runs. Therefore, only the latest day's
returns remain.
• write(b) adds no line separator. Multiple book names are concatenated together, making the log difficult to read.
• If write() raises an exception before close(), the explicit close() line is skipped. The file can remain open until garbage
collection/process exit.
• process() reads the entire daily file and does not close it explicitly. It catches only FileNotFoundError, so other I/O
failures are unhandled.
• The exception handler prints 'missing' but does not save the error in a persistent error log.
