Alternative concept and complexity
If duplicates are detected by searching a list of all previously accepted register numbers, the i-th registration may require
scanning up to i-1 earlier values. Across n registrations, total work is O(n²) in the worst case. A set provides O(1)
average membership/insertion, making the full pass O(n) average, excluding event/output work. Both approaches store
O(n) register identifiers; the set usually has higher per-item overhead but much faster lookup.
